# Native build output for apps with a checked-in native project (currently
# only apps/passenger/android — a bare-workflow Android build). This is
# regenerated fresh on every EAS build, so uploading a stale local copy is
# pure waste. Without this, a leftover debug APK from a previous local
# `expo run:android` sits alongside the freshly-built release APK after the
# remote build runs (assembleRelease doesn't clean first), leaving EAS
# unable to identify a single installable artifact — it falls back to
# tarring both together instead of serving a clean .apk. That tar.gz isn't
# directly installable on Android and is nearly double the size, which made
# it more exposed to CDN download interruptions too.
#
# EAS builds this monorepo from its workspace root (apps/passenger/.easignore
# alone had no effect — the "633 MB" upload size on every build confirmed the
# whole repo root is what gets archived, not the per-app directory), so paths
# here are relative to this root, not to the app being built.
apps/passenger/android/app/build/
apps/passenger/android/build/
apps/passenger/android/.gradle/
apps/passenger/android/.cxx/

# Claude Code's own tooling config — never read by Expo/Gradle/Metro, so it
# has no business in a build upload. .claude/skills/* are real symlinks into
# .agents/skills/*; EAS's local archive step tries to faithfully recreate
# them in its shallow clone and fails with EPERM, since Windows requires
# elevated privileges to create symlinks that this step doesn't have here.
.claude/
.agents/
